@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### Security headers: expect content-security-policy "default-src 'none';..." and x-request-id
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Request id from the client: expect a different x-request-id (a UUID from the API)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live
x-request-id: my-own-id

### Allowed origin: expect 200 and access-control-allow-origin: http://localhost:3000
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Preflight from an allowed origin: expect 204 and access-control-allow-methods
OPTIONS {{baseUrl}}/health/live
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST

### Origin that is not allowed: expect 403 ORIGIN_NOT_ALLOWED
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live
Origin: https://evil.example.net

### Preflight from an origin that is not allowed: expect 403 ORIGIN_NOT_ALLOWED
OPTIONS {{baseUrl}}/health/live
Origin: https://evil.example.net
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST

### Origin null: expect 403 ORIGIN_NOT_ALLOWED
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live
Origin: null

### Write with a cookie and without Origin: expect 403 ORIGIN_REQUIRED
POST {{baseUrl}}/health/live
Cookie: session=test
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Write with a cookie from an allowed origin: expect 404 NOT_FOUND (the check passes, no POST route)
POST {{baseUrl}}/health/live
Cookie: session=test
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Write with only a bearer token: expect 404 NOT_FOUND (the origin check does not apply)
POST {{baseUrl}}/health/live
Authorization: Bearer test
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Prototype poisoning: expect 400 INVALID_BODY
POST {{baseUrl}}/health/live
Content-Type: application/json

{"__proto__": {"isAdmin": true}}

### Bad JSON: expect 400 INVALID_BODY
POST {{baseUrl}}/health/live
Content-Type: application/json

{"a":

# 415 UNSUPPORTED_MEDIA_TYPE and 413 PAYLOAD_TOO_LARGE need a POST route. There is none yet.
# The unit tests check them (apps/api/test/unit/http.test.ts).

### Rate limit: set RATE_LIMIT_MAX=3 in .env, restart the api, send this request 4 times.
# Expect 429 RATE_LIMITED with a Retry-After header on the 4th request.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### API reference (development only): expect 200 and an HTML page. In production: 404.
GET {{baseUrl}}/reference/
